[[64,15,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               monitors\nand controls the entire electronic injection system.</p><p>Engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na supply controlled by the ignition (15/54) at pin 13 of connector\nB from the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B25</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99.</p><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls the system\nsupply: it is supplied by the battery, from the line for maxifuse\nEFI of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99, while the\ncoil is supplied by the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B35</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to\n2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p><p>Pin 46 of connector C of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends\nan enablement signal which energizes the relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends\na supply to the control unit, to pins 7, 8 and 1 of connector A\n(the line which from \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               goes to pin 1 is also protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F3</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99).</p><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is also supplied by\nthe battery from the line of maxifuse EFI of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99\nor of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99;</p><p>pins 30 and 52 of connector C of control\nunit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               send the signals which energize the relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nwhich provides the supply to the fuel pump \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which is\nconnected to earth via the inertia switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>l50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . In case of\nimpact, this cuts off the circuit to prevent the danger of fuel\ndelivery.</p><p>From 2/99: a signal arrives from pin 52\nof connector C of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which energizes the\nrelay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15,</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which provides the supply for the electric fuel pump \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which is earthed via the inertia switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . In\ncase of impact, this cuts off the circuit to prevent the danger\nof fuel delivery.</p><p>The diesel preheating relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J17</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nsupplied by the battery via the line protected by fuses \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B37</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B39</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99, or the GLOW maxifuse of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and the\nfuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fusebox \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99.;\nit receives an ignition-controlled supply (15/54) from the fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B25</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99, and controls the operation of the diesel heating resistor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>O20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              :\nthe thermal contact (connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>O20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) deactivates the\nsystem when heating has taken place.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , responsible for\ncontrolling preheating of heater plugs \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , is supplied directly\nby the battery via a line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B37</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or\nthe GLOW maxifuse of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99. It receives controls\nfrom pins 38 and 51 of connector C of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a feedback\nsignal to pin 1 of connector B of the control unit.</p><p>Pins 4, 5 and 6 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               are\nearthed.</p><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\nsignals from the various sensors in order to monitor all engine\nservice conditions.</p><p>Rpm sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K46</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               supplies information\non engine speed via a frequency signal sent to pin 26 of connector\nD of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives an earth signal from pin\n37 of control unit connector D. Both signals are weak and are therefore\nshielded.</p><p>Timing sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K47</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied from\npin 12 of connector D of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives a\nreference earth from pin 2 of connector D of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends\nit a signal of frequency corresponding to the timing of pin 3 of\nthe same connector.</p>"],[64,15,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>Engine temperature sender unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K45</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              receives\na reference earth from pin 27 of connector D of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsupplies a signal proportional to coolant temperature to pin 36\nof the same connector.</p>"],[64,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>Engine temperature sender unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na reference earth from pin 27 of connector D of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsupplies a signal proportional to coolant temperature to pin 36\nof the same connector. The same sender unit also supplies information\nto the temperature gauge and warning light \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"],[64,15,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>Air flow meter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a general\npower supply from pin 11 of control unit connector D and a reference\nvoltage from pin 1. It sends pin 14 of connector D a signal proportional\nto air flow. \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               also contains an air temperature sensor: the\nsensor reference earth is supplied by pin 4 of connector D of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nwhile an air temperature signal is received by pin 23 of connector\nA.</p><p>Accelerator pedal \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K55</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              is fitted with\ntwo built-in potentiometers (a main one and a safety back-up). The\nfirst receives power and earth from pins 5 and 23 respectively of\nconnector C of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a corresponding signal to pin 10\nof the same connector. The second receives power and earth from\npins 21 and 8 respectively of connector C of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends\na corresponding signal to pin 9 of connector C.</p><p>Fuel temperature sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K81</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               fitted\non the return manifold measures the temperature of diesel leaving\nthe injectors. It receives a reference earth from pin 1 of connector\nC of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a fuel temperature signal to control unit\npin 24.</p><p>The turbocharging sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K82</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               records\nturbo pressure. It is supplied from pin 8 of connector D of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nreceives a reference earth from control unit pin 7. The signal is\nsent to pin 6 of control unit connector D.</p><p>The fuel pressure sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K83</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is responsible\nfor providing the injection control unit with a feedback signal\nfor governing pressure and injection duration. It receives power\nand the reference earth from pins 13 and 34 respectively of connector\nD of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; it then sends the pressure signal to pin 24 of\nthe same connector.</p><p>The fuel pressure regulator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N77</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               has\nthe task of keeping the value of the fuel pressure in the accumulator\nconstant. Both control signals are produced by pins 31 and 21 of\ncontrol unit connector D.</p><p>The EGR solenoid \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls exhaust\ngas recirculation. It is supplied from pin 37 of connector C of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsends a signal to control unit pin 50.</p><p>Pin 8 of connector C of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na signal from brake light switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , ignition-operated (INT)\nthrough a line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               in junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 2 of connector C of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na signal from the clutch pedal switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I31</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , also ignition\noperated (INT) by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receive the opening\ngo ahead supply from pins 2 (cylinders 1 and 4) and 4 (cylinders\n2 and 3) for connector E of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The engine control unit sends commands to\nthe injectors from pins 9, 7, 5 and 3 of connector E for cylinders\n1, 2, 3 and 4, respectively.</p><p>The rev counter module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na supply controlled by the ignition (INT) from the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99: when the earth signal reaches pin\n48 of connector C, the &#x27;injection failure&#x27; warning light comes on.</p><p>The speedometer module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na supply controlled by the ignition (INT) from the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99: when the earth signal reaches pin\n43 of connector C, the &#x27;heater plugs&#x27; warning light comes on.</p><p>The coolant temperature signal is sent to\nthe auxiliary instrument from pin 49 of connector C of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong><a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected to\nthe ALFA ROMEO CODE control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via a line from pin\n13 of connector C; in this way if the ALFA ROMEO CODE unit does\nnot detect a correct code, it does not issue enablement and the\nengine is not started.</p><p>The control unit is equipped with a self-diagnostic\nunit that may be used by connecting the unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via\npin 28 of connector C.</p><p>The speedometer signal (vehicle speed) reaches\npin 26 of connector C of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong><a href=\"#/3234310\">E4021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends out a signal\nproportional to engine rpm \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234270\">E4020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              from\npin 40 of connector C.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected to\nthe air conditioning system via pin 32 of connector D and pin 3\nof connector B. This allows engine idling speed to be adjusted to\nincreased engine load whenever the compressor is activated, or to turn\noff the compressor in the case of high speeds or high engine loads \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234652\">E6021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit also controls the engine\ncooling system: pin 23 of connector B, pin 15 of connector D and\n20, 45 of connector C control activation of the relevant fans \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234439\">E5020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"]]